{
  "id": "bigville_tools",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "depends_on": [],
  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R43 (block 336000): TOOLS + INVENTORY + OWNERSHIP as adventure-game mechanics (USE X ON Z / USE X WITH Y). A tool is an EFFECTIVENESS MULTIPLIER on an action, PHYSICALLY held in an agent's inventory (agent -holds-> tool). Fitness is DATA, not code: tool -fit_for-> Fitness{verb,mult,effort}, so a new tool is a new node, never a new rule. Bare hands attempt anything but bear ALMOST NOTHING at LARGE cost (mult~0.05, effort~3); the right tool WORKS (pick/rod mult 1, effort 1). tl_gather: use a tool on a Deposit -> yield into the matching inventory slot, deposit depleted (conservation). tl_strike: use a tool on a PERSON -> harm = fit.mult. tl_prep: use a tool WITH food -> knife is a SKILL MULTIPLIER. A KNIFE is dual-use (one node, prep+strike fitnesses, verb selects). Tool use is gated on HOLDING, never owning. OWNERSHIP IS A RECOGNIZED FRAME, NOT A WORLD FACT (oc_recognition, mirroring rc_authority): an OwnershipClaim's weight = Count(recognizers). The inn owns its kitchen knives because the town RECOGNIZES the inn's claim -- the cook HOLDS them to work but the recognition sits with the inn. Possession never transfers recognition (a thief holds but does not become owner -> theft); split recognition = disputed ownership the substrate never adjudicates.",
  "nodes": [],
  "edges": [],
  "productions": [],
  "concepts": [],
